<article class="env-definition" id="02RJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02RJ">Definition <span data-tag="02RJ">31.27.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian integral scheme. Let $f \in R(X)^*$. For every prime divisor $Z \subset X$ we define the <em>order of vanishing of $f$ along $Z$</em> as the integer </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{ord}_ Z(f) = \text{ord}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }}(f)  \]
</div>
  <p> where the right hand side is the notion of Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/02MD" data-tag="02MD">10.121.2</a> and $\xi $ is the generic point of $Z$. </p>
</article>